# Post-Incident Review: Service Degradation

## Summary

On 02/06/2026, a service degradation incident affected Example Service, resulting in reduced performance and partial functionality for a subset of users.

The incident was detected via a Splunk monitoring alert and confirmed by an increase in user reports.
Mitigation actions stabilized the service, and full functionality was restored without data loss.

This document summarizes the incident, its impact, contributing factors, and identified follow-up actions.

## Impact

- Affected service: Example Service  
- Impacted users: EMEA Example Service users
- User-facing symptoms:
  - increased response times,
  - intermittent 5xx errors,
  - degraded functionality.
- Business impact:
  - increased customer support volume, 
  - risk of the SLA breach,
  - risk of service discontinuity,
  - internal disruption

